    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0754" n="1712" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1712"/>

                <head>No. 16.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 12, 1889</date>.
                        (Received January 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 893.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring’ to previous correspondence with
                    respect to the dismissal of Lord Sackville, the late British minister at
                    Washington, I have the honor to inclose herewith the official
                        correspondence<anchor n="*" xml:id="d439-f1"/> on the subject issued by Her
                    Majesty’s Government to Parliament, and a copy of an article in this day’s
                    Morning Post.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d439-a1.xml" xpointer="d439-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d439-a2.xml" xpointer="d439-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
